NetHack 3.1 Bugs:

   1)  Graphical glitchiness with pick-axe wielding dwarves, and rockmoles.
   These two fellers seem to disappear invariably after making any movements
   only to reappear if one pulls a ^R (actually all digging monsters).

   2)  Along the same lines as above, when one gets a really good kick on a
   acid blob or small mimic (to name a few of the smaller folk) and kick them
   back a space, two images appear of the said monster.

   3)  Not really a problem with the program but the otherwise useful chredit
   accessory program can't handle the "Rogue/Hack" specialty level.  The
   upper and lower right corner of rooms are X's and W's, up stairs are "l"'s
   etc...

   4)  Do groups of candles give one more or longer light useage than
   just one?  If not I have yet to find a reasonable way to separate the
   candles (other than sacking 'em or just dropping all but one).

   5)  I've also had a few, "Program is in disorder..." while in shops.
   Once it happened while eating tins of spinnach in a shop when all of a
   sudden I became super encumbered even though I hadn't picked up anything
   new at that point and if anything should have been less encumbered since
   my strength just got raised a couple of points.  The other time it seemed
   to freak when it couldn't figure out my bill properly.

   6)  Lastly, the supposed "bug" with the ring of conflict I think makes a
   neat feature.  That ring normally is just too darn powerful without at
   least some drawbacks (above food drainage).

